# A checkout on Windows without core.autocrlf set to "input" (the
# default is "true", which converts working-tree line endings to CRLF)
# would otherwise turn every file below into CRLF text, which breaks two
# different things in two different ways: a shell script's shebang line
# (#!/usr/bin/env bash) with a trailing \r is not the line the kernel's
# script loader recognizes, so testdata/docker/*.sh and testdata/wire/*.sh
# fail to run at all; and testdata/api.golden, compared line by line
# against TestExportedAPI's own output (api_test.go, which tolerates CRLF
# itself as a second line of defense), would otherwise carry a stray \r
# api_test.go never wrote.
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never text-normalized at all, on any platform: this file's lines are
# compared verbatim, one name per line, against the package's own
# exported API (TestExportedAPI, api_test.go).
testdata/api.golden -text
